{"id":"mahabharata-5-162","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":162,"title":"द्विषष्ट्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 162 · Bhishma counts the Kaurava warriors","summary":{"en":"At Duryodhana's request Bhishma assesses the warriors on the Kaurava side, rating each as an atiratha, a maharatha, a ratha or less. He names himself, Duryodhana and his brothers, Kritavarman, Shalya, Bhurishravas, Jayadratha and others, with the deeds each will perform.","kn":"ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಕೋರಿಕೆಯಂತೆ ಭೀಷ್ಮನು ಕೌರವಪಕ್ಷದ ವೀರರನ್ನು ಅತಿರಥ, ಮಹಾರಥ, ರಥ ಅಥವಾ ಕಡಿಮೆ ಎಂದು ಮೌಲ್ಯಮಾಪನ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ತನ್ನನ್ನು, ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಮತ್ತು ಸಹೋದರರನ್ನು, ಕೃತವರ್ಮ, ಶಲ್ಯ, ಭೂರಿಶ್ರವ, ಜಯದ್ರಥ ಮೊದಲಾದವರನ್ನು ಪ್ರತಿಯೊಬ್ಬರು ಮಾಡುವ ಸಾಹಸಗಳೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹೆಸರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"दुर्योधन के अनुरोध पर भीष्म कौरव पक्ष के योद्धाओं का मूल्यांकन करते हैं और प्रत्येक को अतिरथ, महारथ, रथ या उससे कम ठहराते हैं। वे स्वयं, दुर्योधन और उसके भाइयों, कृतवर्मा, शल्य, भूरिश्रवा, जयद्रथ और अन्यों के नाम उनके भावी पराक्रमों सहित बताते हैं।","te":"దుర్యోధనుని కోరికపై భీష్ముడు కౌరవపక్ష వీరులను అతిరథ, మహారథ, రథ లేదా అంతకంటే తక్కువగా అంచనా వేస్తాడు. తనను, దుర్యోధనుడు, సోదరులను, కృతవర్మ, శల్యుడు, భూరిశ్రవసుడు, జయద్రథుడు మొదలైనవారిని ఒక్కొక్కరు చేసే పరాక్రమాలతో పేర్కొంటాడు.","ta":"துரியோதனனின் வேண்டுகோளின்படி பீஷ்மர் கௌரவப் பக்க வீரர்களை அதிரதர், மகாரதர், ரதர் அல்லது அதற்குக் குறைந்தவர் என்று மதிப்பிடுகிறார். தம்மையும், துரியோதனன், சகோதரர்கள், க்ருதவர்மா, ஶல்யன், பூரிஶ்ரவஸ், ஜயத்ரதன் முதலியோரையும் ஒவ்வொருவர் செய்யும் வீரச் செயல்களுடன் பெயரிடுகிறார்.","ml":"ദുര്യോധനന്റെ അഭ്യർഥനപ്രകാരം ഭീഷ്മർ കൗരവപക്ഷത്തെ യോദ്ധാക്കളെ വിലയിരുത്തുന്നു; ഓരോരുത്തരെയും അതിരഥൻ, മഹാരഥൻ, രഥൻ, അതിൽ താഴെ എന്നിങ്ങനെ തരംതിരിക്കുന്നു. തന്നെയും ദുര്യോധനനെയും സഹോദരന്മാരെയും, കൃതവർമ്മാവ്, ശല്യൻ, ഭൂരിശ്രവസ്സ്, ജയദ്രഥൻ എന്നിവരെയും മറ്റുള്ളവരെയും അദ്ദേഹം പേരെടുത്ത് പറയുന്നു; ഓരോരുത്തരും ചെയ്യുന്ന കർമ്മങ്ങളും പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.162; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"रथातिरथसंख्यापर्व","titleEn":"Rathatirathasankhya Parva (Counting the warriors)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"प्रतिज्ञाते फल्गुनेन वधे भीष्मस्य संजय ।\nकिमकुर्वन्त मे मन्दाः पुत्रा दुर्योधनादयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Phalguna had vowed Bhishma's death, Sanjaya, what did my foolish sons led by Duryodhana do?"}},{"n":2,"text":"हतमेव हि पश्यामि गाङ्गेयं पितरं रणे ।\nवासुदेवसहायेन पार्थेन दृढधन्वना ॥","meaning":{"en":"I already see my father Ganga's son slain in battle by Partha of the firm bow, with Vasudeva's help."}},{"n":3,"text":"स चापरिमितप्रज्ञस्तच्छ्रुत्वा पार्थभाषितम् ।\nकिमुक्तवान्महेष्वासो भीष्मः प्रहरतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And hearing what Partha said, what did that man of boundless wisdom, the great archer Bhishma, best of fighters, say?"}},{"n":4,"text":"सेनापत्यं च संप्राप्य कौरवाणां धुरंधरः ।\nकिमचेष्टत गाङ्गेयो महाबुद्धिपराक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And having received the generalship of the Kauravas, as their chief bearer of the load, what did Ganga's son, of great wisdom and valor, do?"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"ततस्तत्संजयस्तस्मै सर्वमेव न्यवेदयत् ।\nयथोक्तं कुरुवृद्धेन भीष्मेणामिततेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Sanjaya told him everything just as the aged Kuru, Bhishma of immeasurable splendor, had said."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"सेनापत्यमनुप्राप्य भीष्मः शांतनवो नृप ।\nदुर्योधनमुवाचेदं वचनं हर्षयन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he received the generalship, Bhishma son of Shantanu spoke these words to Duryodhana, as if delighting him."}},{"n":7,"text":"नमस्कृत्वा कुमाराय सेनान्ये शक्तिपाणये ।\nअहं सेनापतिस्तेऽद्य भविष्यामि न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having bowed to Kumara, spear in hand, the army's leader, I shall be your commander today, without doubt."}},{"n":8,"text":"सेनाकर्मण्यभिज्ञोऽस्मि व्यूहेषु विविधेषु च ।\nकर्म कारयितुं चैव भृतानप्यभृतांस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know the duties of an army and the many battle formations, and how to make men work, paid or unpaid."}},{"n":9,"text":"यात्रायानेषु युद्धेषु लब्धप्रशमनेषु च ।\nभृशं वेद महाराज यथा वेद बृहस्पतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, I know thoroughly marches, advances, battles and the means of peace, as Brihaspati does."}},{"n":10,"text":"व्यूहानपि महारम्भान्दैवगान्धर्वमानुषान् ।\nतैरहं मोहयिष्यामि पाण्डवान्व्येतु ते ज्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will confuse the Pandavas with great formations, divine, gandharva and human; let your fever of worry go."}},{"n":11,"text":"सोऽहं योत्स्यामि तत्त्वेन पालयंस्तव वाहिनीम् ।\nयथावच्छास्त्रतो राजन्व्येतु ते मानसो ज्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So I will fight faithfully, guarding your army according to the rules of the science, king; let your mental fever go."}},{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"न विद्यते मे गाङ्गेय भयं देवासुरेष्वपि ।\nसमस्तेषु महाबाहो सत्यमेतद्ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have no fear, son of Ganga, even of all the gods and demons together; I tell you this truly, mighty-armed one."}},{"n":13,"text":"किं पुनस्त्वयि दुर्धर्षे सेनापत्ये व्यवस्थिते ।\nद्रोणे च पुरुषव्याघ्रे स्थिते युद्धाभिनन्दिनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"How much less when you stand as invincible commander, and Drona, tiger among men, who delights in battle, is there."}},{"n":14,"text":"भवद्भ्यां पुरुषाग्र्याभ्यां स्थिताभ्यां विजयो मम ।\nन दुर्लभं कुरुश्रेष्ठ देवराज्यमपि ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With you two foremost men standing by me, victory is mine; even the kingdom of the gods is surely not hard to win, best of Kurus."}},{"n":15,"text":"रथसंख्यां तु कार्त्स्न्येन परेषामात्मनस्तथा ।\nतथैवातिरथानां च वेत्तुमिच्छामि कौरव ॥","meaning":{"en":"But I wish to know the full count of chariot-warriors on the enemy's side and on our own, and of the atirathas as well, Kaurava."}},{"n":16,"text":"पितामहो हि कुशलः परेषामात्मनस्तथा ।\nश्रोतुमिच्छाम्यहं सर्वैः सहैभिर्वसुधाधिपैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the grandfather is expert about the enemy's side and our own; I wish to hear it, together with all these kings."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"गान्धारे शृणु राजेन्द्र रथसंख्यां स्वके बले ।\nये रथाः पृथिवीपाल तथैवातिरथाश्च ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Gandhari, king of kings, hear the count of chariot-warriors in your own army, those who are rathas and those who are atirathas."}},{"n":18,"text":"बहूनीह सहस्राणि प्रयुतान्यर्बुदानि च ।\nरथानां तव सेनायां यथामुख्यं तु मे शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"There are many thousands, tens of thousands, millions and hundreds of millions of chariots in your army; hear the chief ones from me."}},{"n":19,"text":"भवानग्रे रथोदारः सह सर्वैः सहोदरैः ।\nदुःशासनप्रभृतिभिर्भ्रातृभिः शतसंमितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are in front, a noble chariot-warrior, with all your brothers, Duhshasana and the rest, a hundred in number."}},{"n":20,"text":"सर्वे कृतप्रहरणाश्छेद्यभेद्यविशारदाः ।\nरथोपस्थे गजस्कन्धे गदायुद्धेऽसिचर्मणि ॥","meaning":{"en":"All are skilled with weapons, expert in cutting and piercing, in chariot-fighting, from elephant-back, in mace-fighting and with sword and shield."}},{"n":21,"text":"संयन्तारः प्रहर्तारः कृतास्त्रा भारसाधनाः ।\nइष्वस्त्रे द्रोणशिष्याश्च कृपस्य च शरद्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They can drive, strike, are trained in arms and can bear heavy loads; they are Drona's pupils in archery and Kripa Sharadvata's too."}},{"n":22,"text":"एते हनिष्यन्ति रणे पाञ्चालान्युद्धदुर्मदान् ।\nकृतकिल्बिषाः पाण्डवेयैर्धार्तराष्ट्रा मनस्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These will kill the Panchalas, so fierce in battle; the proud sons of Dhritarashtra are guilty toward the Pandavas."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततोऽहं भरतश्रेष्ठ सर्वसेनापतिस्तव ।\nशत्रून्विध्वंसयिष्यामि कदर्थीकृत्य पाण्डवान् ।\nन त्वात्मनो गुणान्वक्तुमर्हामि विदितोऽस्मि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I, best of Bharatas, as your supreme commander, will destroy your enemies, treating the Pandavas as nothing; yet I will not speak of my own merits, you know me."}},{"n":24,"text":"कृतवर्मा त्वतिरथो भोजः प्रहरतां वरः ।\nअर्थसिद्धिं तव रणे करिष्यति न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kritavarman the Bhoja is an atiratha, best of warriors; he will bring your aims to success in battle, no doubt."}},{"n":25,"text":"अस्त्रविद्भिरनाधृष्यो दूरपाती दृढायुधः ।\nहनिष्यति रिपूंस्तुभ्यं महेन्द्रो दानवानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Invincible to the masters of weapons, he shoots far with a firm weapon, and will kill your enemies as Mahendra killed the danavas."}},{"n":26,"text":"मद्रराजो महेष्वासः शल्यो मेऽतिरथो मतः ।\nस्पर्धते वासुदेवेन यो वै नित्यं रणे रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shalya, the king of Madra, a great archer, I count as an atiratha; he always rivals Vasudeva in every battle."}},{"n":27,"text":"भागिनेयान्निजांस्त्यक्त्वा शल्यस्ते रथसत्तमः ।\nएष योत्स्यति संग्रामे कृष्णं चक्रगदाधरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaving aside his own sister's sons, Shalya your best chariot-warrior will fight Krishna, bearer of discus and mace, in the battle."}},{"n":28,"text":"सागरोर्मिसमैर्वेगैः प्लावयन्निव शात्रवान् ।\nभूरिश्रवाः कृतास्त्रश्च तव चापि हितः सुहृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhurishravas, trained in weapons, also your well-wishing friend, will flood the enemies with a rush like the ocean's waves."}},{"n":29,"text":"सौमदत्तिर्महेष्वासो रथयूथपयूथपः ।\nबलक्षयममित्राणां सुमहान्तं करिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great archer, son of Somadatta, leader of the leaders of chariot-fighters, will cause a huge loss of the enemy's strength."}},{"n":30,"text":"सिन्धुराजो महाराज मतो मे द्विगुणो रथः ।\nयोत्स्यते समरे राजन्विक्रान्तो रथसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of Sindhu, great king, I count as a double chariot-warrior; that valiant best of chariot-fighters will fight in the battle."}},{"n":31,"text":"द्रौपदीहरणे पूर्वं परिक्लिष्टः स पाण्डवैः ।\nसंस्मरंस्तं परिक्लेशं योत्स्यते परवीरहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Earlier, over the abduction of Draupadi, he was harassed by the Pandavas, and remembering that insult he will fight, slayer of enemy heroes."}},{"n":32,"text":"एतेन हि तदा राजंस्तप आस्थाय दारुणम् ।\nसुदुर्लभो वरो लब्धः पाण्डवान्योद्धुमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"For he practiced fierce austerity then, king, and won a very hard boon to fight the Pandavas in battle."}},{"n":33,"text":"स एष रथशार्दूलस्तद्वैरं संस्मरन्रणे ।\nयोत्स्यते पाण्डवांस्तात प्राणांस्त्यक्त्वा सुदुस्त्यजान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Remembering that enmity, dear one, this tiger among chariot-fighters will fight the Pandavas, giving up his life, so hard to give up."}}]}]}